class Solution:
    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
Since the previous ticket failed, I'll be careful here. Pattern p splits into three parts: prefix A, middle B, suffix C (split on the two '*'). A substring matches if it starts with A, ends with C, and contains B between them, in order, with the B occurrence starting at or after the end of A, and C starting at or after the end of B.

Plan:
- Find all occurrences of A, B, C in s using KMP-style search (via `str.find` in a loop would be O(n*m) worst case, so I use KMP prefix function).
- For each start position i of A, find the first B occurrence at position j >= i + len(A), then the first C occurrence at position k >= j + len(B). Candidate length = k + len(C) - i. Take the minimum.
- Use two pointers / bisect over sorted occurrence lists.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-7649", "code": "import bisect\n\nclass Solution:\n    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:\n        parts = p.split('*')\n        A, B, C = parts[0], parts[1], parts[2]\n\n        def occurrences(text, pat):\n            # returns sorted list of start indices where pat occurs in text (KMP)\n            if pat == \"\":\n                return list(range(len(text) + 1))\n            m = len(pat)\n            pi = [0] * m\n            k = 0\n            for i in range(1, m):\n                while k > 0 and pat[i] != pat[k]:\n                    k = pi[k - 1]\n                if pat[i] == pat[k]:\n                    k += 1\n                pi[i] = k\n            res = []\n            k = 0\n            for i, ch in enumerate(text):\n                while k > 0 and ch != pat[k]:\n                    k = pi[k - 1]\n                if ch == pat[k]:\n                    k += 1\n                if k == m:\n                    res.append(i - m + 1)\n                    k = pi[k - 1]\n            return res\n\n        occA = occurrences(s, A)\n        occB = occurrences(s, B)\n        occC = occurrences(s, C)\n        if not occA or not occB or not occC:\n            return -1\n\n        lenA, lenB, lenC = len(A), len(B), len(C)\n        best = -1\n        for i in occA:\n            # first B starting at or after i + lenA\n            jx = bisect.bisect_left(occB, i + lenA)\n            if jx == len(occB):\n                continue\n            j = occB[jx]\n            # first C starting at or after j + lenB\n            kx = bisect.bisect_left(occC, j + lenB)\n            if kx == len(occC):\n                continue\n            k = occC[kx]\n            length = k + lenC - i\n            if best == -1 or length < best:\n                best = length\n        return best\n"}

