class Solution:
    def longestSpecialPath(self, edges: List[List[int]], nums: List[int]) -> List[int]:


=== MODEL ===
Approach: DFS from root 0 maintaining the current root-to-node path. For each node, keep a map from value to the depth (in the path) of its last occurrence on the current path, and the cumulative distance from root. The valid downward paths ending at the current node start just below the nearest previous occurrence of any duplicated value. Use a sliding left boundary: `left` = max over (last occurrence index of nums[v] on path + 1) for the current node. The path from ancestor at depth `left` to current node is special. Maintain prefix-distance and depth arrays along the stack.

Iteratively (to avoid recursion limits), I'll do an explicit DFS with enter/exit events, storing for each value a stack of depths on the current path.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-1232", "code": "from typing import List\n\nclass Solution:\n    def longestSpecialPath(self, edges: List[List[int]], nums: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n        n = len(nums)\n        adj = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n        for u, v, w in edges:\n            adj[u].append((v, w))\n            adj[v].append((u, w))\n\n        # dist[x]: distance from root to x\n        # depth[x]: number of nodes from root to x (1-based count)\n        dist = [0] * n\n        depth = [0] * n\n        parent = [-1] * n\n        # path_nodes: list of node ids on current root-to-node path, indexed by depth\n        path_dist = []  # path_dist[d] = distance of node at depth d (0-indexed from root)\n        # last occurrence depth per value on current path: dict value -> list stack of depths\n        occ = {}\n        # for each node, the start depth (inclusive) of the window of unique values ending at it\n        start = [0] * n\n\n        best_len = 0\n        best_nodes = 0\n        # running \"left\" boundary: window start depth for current path\n        # We recompute per node using saved previous window starts on stack.\n\n        # iterative DFS: stack of (node, state)\n        stack = [(0, 0)]\n        win_left_saved = {}  # node -> left boundary before entering (for restoring)\n        visited = [False] * n\n        visited[0] = True\n        cur_left = [0]  # mutable holder for current window left boundary (depth index)\n\n        while stack:\n            node, state = stack.pop()\n            if state == 0:\n                # enter node\n                d = depth[node]  # depth index of this node (root=0)\n                v = nums[node]\n                prev_left = cur_left[0]\n                win_left_saved[node] = prev_left\n                # last occurrence of v on path (before this node)\n                lst = occ.get(v)\n                if lst:\n                    last_d = lst[-1]\n                    left = max(prev_left, last_d + 1)\n                else:\n                    left = prev_left\n                cur_left[0] = left\n                start[node] = left\n                # window from depth 'left' to d\n                length = dist[node] - (path_dist[left] if left < len(path_dist) else dist[node])\n                if left <= d:\n                    length = dist[node] - (path_dist[left] if left < d else dist[node])\n                nodes_cnt = d - left + 1\n                if length > best_len or (length == best_len and nodes_cnt < best_nodes):\n                    best_len = length\n                    best_nodes = nodes_cnt\n                if best_nodes == 0:\n                    best_nodes = nodes_cnt\n                # push onto path structures\n                if lst is None:\n                    lst = []\n                    occ[v] = lst\n                lst.append(d)\n                # schedule exit\n                stack.append((node, 1))\n                # push children\n                for nb, w in adj[node]:\n                    if not visited[nb]:\n                        visited[nb] = True\n                        parent[nb] = node\n                        dist[nb] = dist[node] + w\n                        depth[nb] = d + 1\n                        stack.append((nb, 0))\n                # maintain path_dist for depth d\n                if len(path_dist) <= d:\n                    path_dist.append(dist[node])\n                else:\n                    path_dist[d] = dist[node]\n            else:\n                # exit node\n                d = depth[node]\n                v = nums[node]\n                occ[v].pop()\n                cur_left[0] = win_left_saved[node]\n\n        return [best_len, best_nodes]\n"}

