class Solution:
    def maxProduct(self, nums: List[int], k: int, limit: int) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
I'll solve this with a DP over the array tracking the state (alternating sum, parity of the subsequence length, product capped by limit). Since nums[i] ≤ 12 and limit ≤ 5000, the product stays bounded: any product > limit is discarded, and zeros need special handling since they make the product 0 regardless of later elements.

